# Security keys allowed to approve Zakura releases.
#
# One line per key: GitHub username, namespace, and the public half of a
# YubiKey-resident key. A signer may list several YubiKeys, such as a backup.
# Each key also needs its YubiKey attestation in .github/release-attestations/,
# named <username>-<key fingerprint>.attestation. Create release accepts an
# approval only if it is signed by a key listed here at the release commit, and
# users verify a published release against this file at its tag.
# Add a key with scripts/enroll-release-key.sh (see docs/release-approval.md).
